  "headline": "Frankie Goes To Hollywood’s 'Relax' Blends Synth-Pop with Timeless Groove",
  "article": "Frankie Goes To Hollywood’s 'Relax' emerged in 1984 as a synth-pop anthem that fused raw energy with infectious hooks, becoming a defining track of the era. The band’s debut single, released in the UK by ZTT Records, initially charted in the Top 75 in November 1983 but didn’t crack the Top 40 until early 1984. Its eventual peak at #10 on the Billboard Hot 100 and 23-week chart run cemented its legacy. The track’s driving rhythm, layered vocals, and provocative lyrics created a sonic blueprint for 1980s pop, blending new wave urgency with danceable grooves. Produced by Trevor Horn, 'Relax' showcased the band’s ability to merge theatricality with mainstream appeal
